{"title":"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12dda010ebddef028cda1ec9d14986f4a26d07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Box$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3ecdfe9d226a4d4f63610504cd529ce1106f6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{\\Box}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e93f297869bd9c9e1d1228abec11a96764eb1ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can first convert the fractions into twelfths, and then add them:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae34cfc269246e54e62a6efc1d5d1e5fbf7d2eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1 \\times 6}{2 \\times 6} = \\frac{6}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4d554ee6d33aa6e5c5ffd6c4d2eb27fcd466fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{4 \\times 3} = \\frac{3}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Adding these, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f163c52895da60cc83d80ae63f6a250b8139051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{6 + 3}{12} = \\frac{9}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since the box simply represents the numerator of the resulting fraction in terms of twelfths, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3cc5855d50feaae968b8f6b1894760778dcf207.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" 